# oxfmt writes LF and has no "preserve existing endings" mode (its `endOfLine` takes lf/crlf/cr —
# Prettier's `"auto"` has no equivalent), so on a CRLF checkout every `npm run format` rewrote all
# 118 files. Nothing wrong reached a commit — the endings normalise on the way in — but the mtime
# churn showed up as phantom `git status` entries and woke every file watcher, and it would have
# become real diffs for anyone with `core.autocrlf=false`. Checking out LF everywhere makes the
# working tree match what the formatter writes, on every platform. Prettier's own docs prescribe
# this same line.
#
# `text=auto` leaves git's binary detection in place, so the PNGs and fonts under assets/ are not
# touched by the eol rule.
* text=auto eol=lf
